@ahmad-paysys - FYI: https://github.com/tazama-lf/tazama-stack/tree/dev/utils#optional-seed-cms-reference_ids

We've added an additional option to the tenant seed script (mostly for the sandbox, but I suspect people might eventually customize it for other implementations) that will also optionally populate the reference_id table for that same tenant. That should at least take care of the immediate problem.

I'm also working on https://github.com/tazama-lf/tazama-stack/issues/283 - this is to drop the migration-container-based setup of the CMS Postgres DB from the tazama-stack in favour of a direct SQL setup scrtipt approach instead (only for the tazama-stack - existing and production deployments should probably still use the container-based migration scripts to accommodate future upgrades - the expectation is that tazama-stack deployments would largely be novel and from scratch, so a migration should not be required by default, and the direct approach will be in line with the direct approach in the /core components as well).
